<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24031" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">in-suesco</span></b> , suēvi,
			suētum, 3, v. n. and <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a.</i> (insuerat,
				<i><span class="en">Tac. A.
				4, 57</span></i>), <i>to accustom</i>, <i>habituate</i> (not in Cic. or Cæs.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Neutr.</i>, <i>to accustom</i> or <i>habituate one</i>'<i>s self</i>, <i>to become accustomed to</i> a thing; constr. with
				dat., with <i>ad</i>, or <i>inf.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b> With <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpori,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 11, 29</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			With <i>ad</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ad disciplinam militiae insuescere militem
					nostrum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv. 5,
					6</span></i>
			.— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			With <i>inf.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mentiri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ter.
					Ad. 1, 1, 30</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">largiri,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sall.
					J. 8, 2</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">amare, potare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					C. 11, 6</span></i>
			. —</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Act.</i>, <i>to accuslom</i> or <i>habituate</i> one <i>to</i> a thing;
			constr. <i>aliquem aliquid</i> or <i>aliqua re.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<i>Aliquem aliquid</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">insuevit pater optimus hoc me Ut fugerem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					S. 1, 4, 105</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			<i>Aliquem aliqua re</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aquā pecus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col. 6,
					4</span></i>
			.—<i>Pass.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sic insuesci debent, ut,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 11,
					3</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ita se a pueris insuetos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					24, 48, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
